      "hints": [
        "Complete the square: $5(y^2 - 6y) + 50 = 5[(y - 3)^2 - 9] + 50$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factor out $5$ from the first two terms and complete the square:\n$$5y^2 - 30y + 50 = 5(y^2 - 6y) + 50 = 5\\left[(y - 3)^2 - 9\\right] + 50 = 5(y - 3)^2 - 45 + 50 = 5(y - 3)^2 + 5$$\nwhere $a = -3$ and $b = 5$."
      ],
